---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout
  title="Tipiṭaka Comparative Markdown Edition — tipitaka-md.github.io"
  description="Comparative digital viewer for Pāḷi Tipiṭaka Markdown editions (World Tipiṭaka 2500, Pali Text Society, Buddha Jayanthi, Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana CST4, and Siam Rath) with Rosely text variant highlighting and multi-script transliteration."
  lang="en"
>
  <main>
    <div class="hero-banner">
      <h1>Tipiṭaka Comparative Markdown Edition</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Multi-Edition Comparative Digital Viewer for Canonical Pāḷi Texts in Markdown with
        Rosely Text Variant Diffing &amp; Multi-Script Transliteration
      </p>
      <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; justify-content: center; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 1.5rem;">
        <a href="/reader.html?book=6D&sutta=dn1" class="btn-primary" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.65rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; color: #fff; background-color: var(--primary-color);">
          <span>🚀 Launch Comparative Reader (DN 1)</span>
        </a>
        <a href="/reader.html?book=6D" class="btn-secondary" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.65rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); color: var(--text-body); background-color: var(--bg-tertiary);">
          <span>📚 Browse Books</span>
        </a>
        <a href="https://github.com/tipitaka-md" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" style="display: inline-flex; align-items: center; gap: 0.5rem; padding: 0.65rem 1.4rem; border-radius: 8px; font-weight: 600; text-decoration: none; border: 1px solid var(--border-color); color: var(--text-body); background-color: var(--bg-body);">
          <span>↗ View GitHub Repos</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="home-intro-layout">
      <div>
        <p>
          <strong>tipitaka-md.github.io</strong> provides an interactive comparative reading environment
          for the Theravāda Buddhist Canon across five international standard editions converted into
          plain, version-controlled <strong>Markdown format</strong>. Using <strong>The World Tipiṭaka
          Edition (B.E. 2500 / 2020 Edition)</strong> as the canonical base, this viewer allows scholars,
          students, and practitioners to cross-examine textual variants, orthographical traditions,
          and readings in real time.
        </p>
        <p>
          Derived from the architecture of <a href="https://tipitaka2500.github.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>tipitaka2500.github.io</strong></a>
          and styled using the <a href="https://rosely.hellotham.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Rosely Design System</strong></a>,
          the viewer highlights textual differences dynamically using harmonic Rosely color tokens:
        </p>

        <div style="display: flex; gap: 0.75rem; flex-wrap: wrap; margin: 1.25rem 0;">
          <span class="legend-badge legend-add" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; font-size: 0.88rem; border-radius: 6px;">
            ● Light Green (Spearmint #64bfa4): Textual Addition
          </span>
          <span class="legend-badge legend-change" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; font-size: 0.88rem; border-radius: 6px;">
            ● Light Yellow (Meadowlark #eada4f): Word Variant / Change
          </span>
          <span class="legend-badge legend-del" style="padding: 0.4rem 0.8rem; font-size: 0.88rem; border-radius: 6px;">
            ● Light Pink (Rose Quartz #f7caca): Omission / Deletion
          </span>
        </div>

        <p style="margin-bottom: 0;">
          Select any book from the sidebar, compare two editions side-by-side with synchronized scrolling,
          or transliterate dynamically between <strong>Roman (IAST)</strong>, <strong>Sinhala (සිංහල)</strong>,
          <strong>Thai (ไทย)</strong>, <strong>Burmese (မြန်မာ)</strong>, and <strong>Devanagari (देवनागरी)</strong>.
        </p>
      </div>

      <figure class="home-volume-figure">
        <picture>
          <source type="image/webp" srcset="/images/tipitaka-volumes.webp" />
          <img
            src="/images/tipitaka-volumes.jpg"
            alt="The 40 volumes of the Roman-script World Tipiṭaka Edition arranged in a circle"
            width="743"
            height="575"
            fetchpriority="high"
            class="home-volume-img"
          />
        </picture>
        <figcaption class="home-volume-caption">
          Comparative collation across 5 international editions of the <em>Tipiṭaka</em>
        </figcaption>
      </figure>
    </div>

    <!-- Quick Sutta Launcher -->
    <section aria-label="Canonical Highlights &amp; Sutta Launcher" style="margin: 2.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--text-emphasis); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding-bottom: 0.5rem;">
        ⚡ Canonical Highlights &amp; Sutta Directory
      </h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        Jump straight into key discourses with multi-edition cross-referencing and Rosely diff highlighting active:
      </p>

      <div class="home-index-grid">
        <a href="/reader.html?book=6D&sutta=dn1" class="home-index-card">
          <div>
            <h2>DN 1 Brahmajālasutta</h2>
            <p>
              The Supreme Net of Views: classification of all 62 philosophical and cosmological
              doctrines of ancient India.
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="home-index-stat">Compare 5 Editions →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/reader.html?book=6D&sutta=dn2" class="home-index-card">
          <div>
            <h2>DN 2 Sāmaññaphalasutta</h2>
            <p>
              The Fruits of the Contemplative Life: King Ajātasattu inquires about the tangible
              benefits of monastic training.
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="home-index-stat">Compare 5 Editions →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/reader.html?book=7D&sutta=dn16" class="home-index-card">
          <div>
            <h2>DN 16 Mahāparinibbānasutta</h2>
            <p>
              The Great Passing of the Buddha: final journey from Rājagaha to Kusinārā, instructions
              to Ānanda, and the Four Great Authorities.
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="home-index-stat">Compare 5 Editions →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/reader.html?book=9M&sutta=mn10" class="home-index-card">
          <div>
            <h2>MN 10 Satipaṭṭhānasutta</h2>
            <p>
              The Direct Path to Liberation: the Four Foundations of Mindfulness (body, feelings,
              mind, and mental qualities).
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="home-index-stat">Compare 5 Editions →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/reader.html?book=14S5&sutta=sn56_11" class="home-index-card">
          <div>
            <h2>SN 56.11 Dhammacakkappavattana</h2>
            <p>
              Setting the Wheel of Dhamma in Motion: the first sermon at the Deer Park in Bārāṇasī,
              the Middle Way, and the Four Noble Truths.
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="home-index-stat">Compare 5 Editions →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/reader.html?book=18Dh" class="home-index-card">
          <div>
            <h2>KN 2 Dhammapada</h2>
            <p>
              Treasury of Truth: 423 beloved aphorisms and verses of canonical Buddhist wisdom arranged
              in 26 chapters (vaggas).
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="home-index-stat">Compare 5 Editions →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/reader.html?book=1V" class="home-index-card">
          <div>
            <h2>1V Pārājikapāḷi</h2>
            <p>
              The Vinaya Monastic Rules of Defeat: origin stories and formulation of the major rules
              for Buddhist monks (Bhikkhu Vinaya).
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="home-index-stat">Compare 5 Editions →</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/reader.html?book=34Dh" class="home-index-card">
          <div>
            <h2>34Dh Dhammasaṅgaṇī</h2>
            <p>
              Enumeration of Phenomena: the foundational philosophical book of the Abhidhammapiṭaka,
              analyzing mind, consciousness, and matter.
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="home-index-stat">Compare 5 Editions →</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- The 5 Editions Grid -->
    <section aria-label="The Five Comparative Editions" style="margin: 2.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--text-emphasis); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding-bottom: 0.5rem;">
        📖 The Five Canonical Editions in Markdown
      </h2>
      <p style="color: var(--text-secondary); margin-bottom: 1.25rem;">
        Each edition is independently hosted and maintained in clean GitHub repositories:
      </p>

      <div class="home-index-grid">
        <a
          href="https://github.com/tipitaka-md/tipitaka2500"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="home-index-card"
        >
          <div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary-color); margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
              BASE REFERENCE EDITION
            </div>
            <h2>🌟 World Tipiṭaka 2500 (T2500)</h2>
            <p>
              The 40-volume Roman-script World Tipiṭaka Edition (B.E. 2500 / 2020 Edition), collated by canonical
              scholars against 18 international editions with comprehensive critical apparatus variant footnotes.
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="home-index-stat">tipitaka-md/tipitaka2500 ↗</span>
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://github.com/tipitaka-md/pts"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="home-index-card"
        >
          <div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; color: #165b48; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
              LONDON / GRETIL EDITION
            </div>
            <h2>🇬🇧 Pali Text Society (PTS)</h2>
            <p>
              The pioneering European Roman-script edition founded by T.W. Rhys Davids in 1881. Converted from
              GRETIL archival plain text with structured Markdown headers, section divisions, and clean typography.
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="home-index-stat">tipitaka-md/pts ↗</span>
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://github.com/tipitaka-md/buddha-jayanthi"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="home-index-card"
        >
          <div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; color: #85677b; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
              SRI LANKA B.E. 2500 COMMEMORATION
            </div>
            <h2>🇱🇰 Buddha Jayanthi (BJT)</h2>
            <p>
              The official Sri Lankan Government 57-volume Buddha Jayanthi Tripitaka Series (1956–1989). Converted
              from SuttaCentral / AP95 Unicode sources with preserved BJT volume and page numbering anchors.
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="home-index-stat">tipitaka-md/buddha-jayanthi ↗</span>
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://github.com/tipitaka-md/cst"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="home-index-card"
        >
          <div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; color: #695d08; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
              SIXTH BUDDHIST COUNCIL (CST4)
            </div>
            <h2>🇲🇲 Chaṭṭha Saṅgāyana (CST)</h2>
            <p>
              The authoritative Sixth Buddhist Council text (1954–1956, Yangon, Myanmar) digitized by the Vipassana
              Research Institute (VRI). Converted deterministically from tipitaka-xml covering Mūla, Aṭṭhakathā, and Ṭīkā.
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="home-index-stat">tipitaka-md/cst ↗</span>
        </a>

        <a
          href="https://github.com/tipitaka-md/siam-rath"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="home-index-card"
        >
          <div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; color: #96254a; margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
              ROYAL THAI EDITION (RAMA VII)
            </div>
            <h2>🇹🇭 Siam Rath (Syāmaraṭṭha)</h2>
            <p>
              The prestigious 45-volume Royal Thai Syāmaraṭṭha Tepiṭakaṃ printed under King Prajadhipok (Rama VII, 1925–1928).
              Converted deterministically from D-tipitaka with Thai volume &amp; item numbering.
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="home-index-stat">tipitaka-md/siam-rath ↗</span>
        </a>

        <a href="/reader.html?book=6D" class="home-index-card" style="border-style: dashed;">
          <div>
            <div style="font-size: 0.85rem; font-weight: 700; color: var(--primary-color); margin-bottom: 0.35rem;">
              INTERACTIVE VIEWER
            </div>
            <h2>⚡ Open Comparative Reader</h2>
            <p>
              Launch the multi-pane reading shell. Compare any book or sutta side-by-side with synchronized scrolling,
              Rosely variant diffing, and live script transliteration.
            </p>
          </div>
          <span class="home-index-stat">Open Reader →</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Rosely Design System & Methodology -->
    <section aria-label="Rosely Design &amp; Methodology" style="margin: 2.5rem 0 2rem;">
      <h2 style="font-size: 1.35rem; font-weight: 700; margin: 0 0 1rem; color: var(--text-emphasis); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border-color); padding-bottom: 0.5rem;">
        🎨 Rosely Text Variant Highlighting System
      </h2>
      <div style="background-color: var(--bg-secondary); border: 1px solid var(--border-color); border-radius: 8px; padding: 1.5rem; margin-top: 1rem;">
        <p style="margin-top: 0;">
          Textual variants in Pali manuscripts (such as orthographical differences between <em>Evaṁ</em> and <em>Evaṃ</em>,
          or phrase-level expansions and omissions) are highlighted in real-time using colors sampled directly from the
          <a href="https://rosely.hellotham.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer"><strong>Rosely Design System</strong></a>:
        </p>
        <ul style="line-height: 1.8; margin-bottom: 0.5rem;">
          <li>
            <strong style="color: #165b48;">Spearmint (<code>roselyD</code> #64bfa4)</strong>: Identifies words or phrases present in the comparative edition but absent in the base World Tipiṭaka text.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong style="color: #695d08;">Meadowlark (<code>roselyF</code> #eada4f)</strong>: Identifies variant spellings, word inflections, or altered grammatical forms. Hovering over the highlighted word displays the reading from the base text.
          </li>
          <li>
            <strong style="color: #96254a;">Rose Quartz (<code>rosely5</code> #f7caca / <code>rosely4</code> #ec809e)</strong>: Identifies words present in the base text that have been omitted or omitted in the comparative edition.
          </li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </section>

    <p style="margin-top: 2rem;">
      This website is created and maintained by <strong>Chris Tham</strong> (<a href="mailto:chris@christham.net">chris@christham.net</a>),
      author of the online <a href="https://christham.net/buddhavacana/pali-textbook/0-status/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Pāḷi Textbook</a>.
    </p>
    <p>
      <img src="/images/cc-zero.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true" width="16" height="16" class="cc-icon" />
      CC0: This work has been marked as dedicated to the public domain.{' '}
      <a href="https://creativecommons.org/publicdomain/zero/1.0/">See the CC0 Deed</a>.
    </p>
  </main>
</Layout>
